    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0809" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg723"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No official record of the substance of this meeting has been found, and the only
                    reference to it appears in Hopkins’ notes of January 24, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg839">p. 839</ref>. According to Hopkins,
                    Macmillan brought news that de Gaulle insisted on the dominant role in the
                    French movement. After conferring with Roosevelt, Hopkins informed Macmillan
                    that it was up to Churchill to bring de Gaulle to a meeting with Giraud.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
